{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0d9b43a9-f8cc-49bc-a912-df9d9ee230ac","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8798b14f875509f2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-62sgyse7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Scoping Model for the Default Vector Store\n\n## Description\n\nDetermines the scoping model for the default pgvector-backed vector store in multi-tenant environments — per namespace, per OGX (Llama Stack) instance, or both — and what the choice means for isolation, resource overhead, and lifecycle ownership. The strategy records the Gen AI Studio lead's preference for per-namespace isolation; the per-instance concern originally stemmed from Auto Rag, which is now out of this strategy's scope (addressed in RHAISTRAT-7824). The outcome rewrites what the provisioning implementations build and what the end-to-end validation verifies.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Analyze how playground OGXServer instances map to namespaces under the current gen-ai BFF provisioning model (the BFF creates OGXServer instances for the playground).\n- Evaluate per-namespace vs per-OGX-instance vs a supported combination: multi-tenant isolation guarantees, PostgreSQL instance proliferation, resource overhead in resource-constrained environments, and lifecycle ownership (who creates, who cleans up).\n- Recommend one scoping model (or supported combination) with the isolation and resource trade-off rationale, for consumption by the default-vector-store provisioning implementation and the end-to-end validation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A decision record recommends one scoping model (or a supported combination) with explicit isolation and resource-trade-off rationale.\n- The recommendation addresses multi-tenant isolation (the strategy's per-namespace example) and resource overhead in resource-constrained environments.\n- The recommendation states the lifecycle-ownership consequences of the chosen model (which actor owns creation and cleanup of the provisioned instance).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- REQ-5: default vector store scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (e.g., per-namespace isolation).\n- Informs REQ-6 (lightweight footprint) via the instance-proliferation analysis.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":102387,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcdcfbfb0101f62c","agent_id":"a064da097f30cb08b","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"34aa6925-93c7-4c6a-81d6-430f1fbf0a28","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:35:00.632Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
