{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c1b68c61-48f5-49e8-956b-abda724c4ca2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a31c5461863edfdc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-62sgyse7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E003.md","content":"# Migration Path from the Default Vector Store to Production Vector Databases\n\n## Description\n\nDecides whether users need an explicit migration path from the default (development-experimentation-grade) vector store to a production-grade vector database, and in what form. Context: the Staff Engineer Input positions the default pgvector instance for development experimentation, with users holding production-scale vector workloads directed to an external vector database; a stakeholder raised the importance of aligning with commonly-used vector DB providers for easier migration. The answer determines whether a migration-path implementation epic exists.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Determine what migration would mean for the default store's typical usage (small document sets, development experimentation): for example re-ingestion of source documents against a new vector database versus data export.\n- Assess alignment with the commonly-used vector DB providers already supported by the OGX vector I/O provider surface (pgvector, Milvus, Qdrant backends).\n- Recommend one of two bounded outcomes: provide a migration path (specifying its form and scope sufficiently to plan the implementation), or documentation-only guidance (default store positioned as development-experimentation-grade; production workloads directed to external vector databases).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A recommendation exists with rationale, covering the product expectation for users who outgrow the default vector store.\n- If a migration path is affirmed, its form and scope are specified well enough to plan the follow-up implementation.\n- If no migration path is recommended, the documentation-only positioning is specified so it can be folded into the delivered default-store capability.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- REQ-11: migration path from the default vector store to a production-grade vector database (strategy open question).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":102953,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcdcfbfb0101f62c","agent_id":"a064da097f30cb08b","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"ba57f25d-e403-4b72-95be-143d8878aa61","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:35:08.536Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
