{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7554951c-c0b2-456f-87f0-6ab0506a1022","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9283b1d6caa3f999","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-62sgyse7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E004.md","content":"# Inline Milvus Baseline and pgvector Default Vector Store Benchmark\n\n## Description\n\nCaptures the performance baseline of the current inline Milvus vector store provider and benchmarks the remote pgvector vector I/O provider against it on representative Gen AI Studio playground RAG workloads, verifying that pgvector is in the same order of magnitude. Also records PostgreSQL resource-sizing observations against the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource requests/limits starting point. This is Tier 1 risk-reduction work: it does not depend on the provisioning-approach decision, and the inline baseline must be captured while inline providers still exist in the OGX distribution image (they are removed by RHAISTRAT-7474).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Capture the inline Milvus provider baseline on representative playground RAG workloads (typical usage involves small document sets).\n- Benchmark the OGX remote pgvector vector I/O provider on the same workloads, backed by a standalone PostgreSQL/pgvector instance using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that already includes pgvector (no custom image build, no Konflux onboarding).\n- Use flat scan (no index) for the default store — sufficient for development-experimentation usage; do not evaluate index-type selection or corpus-size ranges (resolved out of scope by Staff Engineer Input).\n- Compare results: verify pgvector is in the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline; strict latency SLAs (p50/p95/p99 thresholds) are explicitly not required.\n- Record resource-usage observations for PostgreSQL/pgvector sizing relative to the model-registry-operator's resource requests/limits reference.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The benchmark report documents the inline Milvus baseline captured from the current inline provider while it is still available in the distribution image.\n- The benchmark report documents pgvector measurements on identical workloads and states the same-order-of-magnitude comparison result.\n- The benchmark report records resource-usage observations against the model-registry-operator PostgreSQL sizing reference.\n- The benchmark harness (scripts, workload definitions, configuration) is retained and reproducible.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- REQ-6: default vector store lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments (sizing observations against the reference).\n- Contributes to REQ-2: playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability (performance-parity evidence).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Cross-strategy timing risk: the inline Milvus baseline must be captured before RHAISTRAT-7474 removes inline providers from the OGX distribution image. If that removal lands first, reconstruct the baseline from a pinned pre-removal image.\n- The sizing findings feed the provisioning implementations as an acceptance-criterion gate (resource requests/limits start from the model-registry-operator reference and are adjusted per these findings), not as a blocking dependency — the benchmark and the gated provisioning work run in parallel.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":103481,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcdcfbfb0101f62c","agent_id":"a064da097f30cb08b","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"86847b39-3c1b-4032-b3c2-d27a2c9542d8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:35:18.392Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
