{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-6b484316-2c45-4b07-a001-ac1ec70bb230","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-97a69b3f36c4cfdd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-62sgyse7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E005.md","content":"# End-to-End Validation of Gen AI Studio Playground RAG with the Default Vector Store\n\n## Description\n\nValidates, end to end, that Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default pgvector-backed vector store with no loss of current capability, once the selected provisioning approach has delivered an instance. Verifies the out-of-the-box experience (no manual setup), multi-tenant scoping, decoupling of the vector store from the OGX instance (separate process, not an inline provider), and performance consistent with the benchmark findings. Scoped to Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows only — Auto Rag compatibility is handled in RHAISTRAT-7824.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Execute playground RAG workflows (document ingestion, vector storage and retrieval, grounded generation) against the default vector store delivered by the selected provisioning approach.\n- Verify functional parity with the current inline-provider experience: no loss of current capability, using a parity checklist plus the benchmark's performance evidence.\n- Verify multi-tenant scoping behavior per the selected scoping model (e.g., per-namespace isolation).\n- Verify the default vector store runs as a separate process decoupled from the OGX instance.\n- Verify the out-of-the-box experience: no additional manual setup steps for RAG workflows compared to the current experience.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Validation is executed against an instance delivered by the selected provisioning approach, available and configured in the target namespace (this coupling to the selected delivery is an acceptance gate on this epic, not a dependency on any specific implementation).\n- Functional parity: every playground RAG capability that works with the current inline vector store works with the default vector store.\n- Multi-tenant scoping is verified per the selected scoping model.\n- The default vector store is confirmed to run as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n- No additional manual setup steps are required for playground RAG workflows.\n- A validation report is published with results, evidence, and any follow-up findings.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- REQ-2: Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability.\n- REQ-4: default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance.\n- REQ-5: multi-tenant scoping verification.\n- REQ-7: no functional regression and no additional manual setup versus the current experience.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":104252,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcdcfbfb0101f62c","agent_id":"a064da097f30cb08b","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"bd1db97c-09e0-440f-80b2-6e22f579fa38","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:35:26.795Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
