{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0e22b87c-4de7-4648-9137-6e2cc98b2055","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad5747f4a75f5b00","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-62sgyse7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E006.md","content":"# Operator-Based Self-Provisioning of the Default pgvector Vector Store\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the default vector store for the Gen AI Studio playground by extending the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer (delivered by the dashboard operator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164) with PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management, following the model-registry-operator pattern: the operator provisions and manages a PostgreSQL instance — using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that already includes pgvector (no custom image build, no Konflux onboarding) — and the gen-ai BFF configures playground OGXServer instances to use the remote pgvector vector I/O provider backed by it. This branch is selected when the go/no-go decision confirms the operator layer lands in time for RHOAI 3.5.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Operator-layer PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management (provisioning, connection-secret delivery, upgrades, cleanup) following the model-registry-operator pattern for auto-provisioned databases; the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry this RHOAI-specific logic.\n- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that ships pgvector; resource requests/limits start from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing and are adjusted per the benchmark findings.\n- Implement the scoping model selected by the scoping investigation (per-namespace isolation preferred).\n- Gen-ai BFF wiring: playground OGXServer instances are configured with the remote pgvector vector I/O provider connected to the operator-provisioned database; OGX application storage remains on its existing SQLite default (vector storage 