iguration produces actionable feedback in the playground.\n- Documentation covers the setup end to end with no undocumented manual steps.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- REQ-2: playground RAG workflows function (with the user-provided vector store).\n- REQ-4: the vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n- Partial REQ-1/REQ-7 coverage only, by design: this branch accepts manual setup as the documented 3.5 fallback per the Staff Engineer Input; the out-of-the-box experience is restored by the platform-provided shared database direction in RHOAI 3.6.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- This branch exists only if the go/no-go decision selects the bring-your-own fallback; it is the last-resort outcome, not the preferred one.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":106953,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcdcfbfb0101f62c","agent_id":"a064da097f30cb08b","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"7b720247-8acc-4fef-956c-f2af379a9627","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:35:57.497Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
