{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-927d0a7cb0ba29b4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Migration path from the default vector store to production vector databases\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Migration Path from the Default Vector Store to Production Vector Databases\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDecides whether users need an explicit migration path from the default (development-experimentation-grade) vector store to a production-grade vector database, and in what form. Context: the Staff Engineer Input positions the default pgvector instance for development experimentation, with users holding production-scale vector workloads directed to an external vector database; a stakeholder raised the importance of aligning with commonly-used vector DB providers for easier migration. The answer determines whether a migration-path implementation epic exists.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Determine what migration would mean for the default store's typical usage (small document sets, development experimentation): for example re-ingestion of source documents against a new vector database versus data export.\n34\t- Assess alignment with the commonly-used vector DB providers already supported by the OGX vector I/O provider surface (pgvector, Milvus, Qdrant backends).\n35\t- Recommend one of two bounded outcomes: provide a migration path (specifying its form and scope sufficiently to plan the implementation), or documentation-only guidance (default store positioned as development-experimentation-grade; production workloads directed to external vector databases).\n36\t\n37\t## Acceptance Criteria\n38\t\n39\t- A recommendation exists with rationale, covering the product expectation for users who outgrow the default vector store.\n40\t- If a migration path is affirmed, its form and scope are specified well enough to plan the follow-up implementation.\n41\t- If no migration path is recommended, the documentation-only positioning is specified so it can be folded into the delivered default-store capability.\n42\t\n43\t## HLR Traceability\n44\t\n45\t- REQ-11: migration path from the default vector store to a production-grade vector database (strategy open question).\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99a250d43d96258d","agent_id":"a46add88d99ec933a","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"fc4309e4-103b-4dcc-9578-05f65aff0ae1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:38:54.866Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-927d0a7cb0ba29b4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
