{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d23a524e8ab2bd7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E006\n3\ttitle: Customer-provided PostgreSQL support for playground RAG\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the go/no-go decision selects a self-provisioning approach\n17\t    (operator-based or BFF-managed), this epic is not implemented; only the external-database\n18\t    escape-hatch support may be retained as part of the selected branch.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 5\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Customer-Provided PostgreSQL Support for Playground RAG\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDegraded fallback for RHOAI 3.5, selected only if the go/no-go decision rules out both self-provisioning approaches: require customers to bring their own PostgreSQL for RAG capabilities in the playground. Users manually configure the OGXServer CR spec with their PostgreSQL connection details — aligning with the breaking changes introduced in OGX 1.0 — while the playground continues to abstract OGX from users where possible. This branch deliberately does not preserve the out-of-the-box experience; that degradation is accepted explicitly by the go/no-go decision.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Support user-supplied PostgreSQL connection details (explicit connection string secret) on playground OGXServer instances, with the remote pgvector vector I/O provider configured against the user's database.\n44\t- Surface actionable validation and errors in the playground when connection details are missing or invalid (playground RAG requires a vector store once inline providers are removed from the distribution).\n45\t- User-facing documentation for configuring a PostgreSQL database with pgvector for playground RAG, aligned with the OGX 1.0 breaking-change posture.\n46\t- Document positioning guidance: the default-store capability is development-experimentation grade, and guidance for choosing a production-grade vector database.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- A user-configured PostgreSQL connection (supplied via secret) is honored by the playground's OGXServer instance, and playground RAG workflows function against it.\n51\t- Missing or invalid connection configuration produces actionable feedback in the playground.\n52\t- Documentation covers the setup end to end with no undocumented manual steps.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- REQ-2: playground RAG workflows function (with the user-provided vector store).\n57\t- REQ-4: the vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n58\t- Partial REQ-1/REQ-7 coverage only, by design: this branch accepts manual setup as the documented 3.5 fallback per the Staff Engineer Input; the out-of-the-box experience is restored by the platform-provided shared database direction in RHOAI 3.6.\n59\t\n60\t## Risks / Notes\n61\t\n62\t- This branch exists only if the go/no-go decision selects the bring-your-own fallback; it is the last-resort outcome, not the preferred one.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6e723cc7b26cd0d","agent_id":"aa8f64a754387b1a3","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"287fdd38-c395-4f46-9adc-b4c2396d2233","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:46:14.969Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d23a