{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b74be4acd312632a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Scoping model for the default vector store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Scoping Model for the Default Vector Store\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDetermines the scoping model for the default pgvector-backed vector store in multi-tenant environments — per namespace, per OGX (Llama Stack) instance, or both — and what the choice means for isolation, resource overhead, and lifecycle ownership. The strategy records the Gen AI Studio lead's preference for per-namespace isolation; the per-instance concern originally stemmed from Auto Rag, which is now out of this strategy's scope (addressed in RHAISTRAT-7824). The outcome rewrites what the provisioning implementations build and what the end-to-end validation verifies.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Analyze how playground OGXServer instances map to namespaces under the current gen-ai BFF provisioning model (the BFF creates OGXServer instances for the playground).\n34\t- Evaluate per-namespace vs per-OGX-instance vs a supported combination: multi-tenant isolation guarantees, PostgreSQL instance proliferation, resource overhead in resource-constrained environments, and lifecycle ownership (who creates, who cleans up).\n35\t- Recommend one scoping model (or supported combination) with the isolation and resource trade-off rationale, for consumption by the default-vector-store provisioning implementation and the end-to-end validation.\n36\t\n37\t## Acceptance Criteria\n38\t\n39\t- A decision record recommends one scoping model (or a supported combination) with explicit isolation and resource-trade-off rationale.\n40\t- The recommendation addresses multi-tenant isolation (the strategy's per-namespace example) and resource overhead in resource-constrained environments.\n41\t- The recommendation states the lifecycle-ownership consequences of the chosen model (which actor owns creation and cleanup of the provisioned instance).\n42\t\n43\t## HLR Traceability\n44\t\n45\t- REQ-5: default vector store scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (e.g., per-namespace isolation).\n46\t- Informs REQ-6 (lightweight footprint) via the instance-proliferation analysis.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6e723cc7b26cd0d","agent_id":"aa8f64a754387b1a3","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"2856dc97-e56c-4aec-b750-6eed5847a0a7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:46:19.820Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b74be4acd312632a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
