{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-845f431deaf729c7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Operator-based self-provisioning of the default pgvector vector store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the RHOAI-controlled operator layer (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n17\t    not land in time for RHOAI 3.5, provisioning moves to the BFF-managed or bring-your-own\n18\t    branch; the operator-based lifecycle design does not ship in 3.5 and may move\n19\t    to 3.6 aligned with the platform-provided shared database.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 0\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: -1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: -1\n27\t  human_process_gates: 0\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: Medium\n33\tai_implementability_score: 1\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator-Based Self-Provisioning of the Default pgvector Vector Store\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tDelivers the default vector store for the Gen AI Studio playground by extending the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer (delivered by the dashboard operator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164) with PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management, following the model-registry-operator pattern: the operator provisions and manages a PostgreSQL instance — using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that already includes pgvector (no custom image build, no Konflux onboarding) — and the gen-ai BFF configures playground OGXServer instances to use the remote pgvector vector I/O provider backed by it. This branch is selected when the go/no-go decision confirms the operator layer lands in time for RHOAI 3.5.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Operator-layer PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management (provisioning, connection-secret delivery, upgrades, cleanup) following the model-registry-operator pattern for auto-provisioned databases; the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry this RHOAI-specific logic.\n45\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that ships pgvector; resource requests/limits start from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing and are adjusted per the benchmark findings.\n46\t- Implement the scoping model selected by the scoping investigation (per-namespace isolation preferred).\n47\t- Gen-ai BFF wiring: playground OGXServer instances are configured with the remote pgvector vector I/O provider connected to the operator-provisioned database; OGX application storage remains on its existing SQLite default (vector storage and application storage are independent configurations — no consolidation, no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL application-storage migration).\n48\t- Reuse the existing OGX remote vector store implementation; no OGX distribution code change is expected, and provider behavior is validated as an acceptance criterion.\n49\t- Document the default store's positioning: development-experimentation grade, with production-scale vector workloads directed to an external vector database.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A PostgreSQL/pgvector instance is provisioned and managed by the operator, with credentials delivered via a secret; provisioning and cleanup happen without manual intervention.\n54\t- Playground OGXServer instances use the remote pgvector vector I/O provider backed by the provisioned database; OGX application storage remains SQLite.\n55\t- Resource requests/limits follow the model-registry-operator starting point, adjusted per the benchmark findings.\n56\t- Scoping follows the selected scoping model (per-namespace isolation unless the decision differs).\n57\t- Escape hatch / rollback path: the playground can be pointed at an externally provisioned vector database, so the default store is not a single point of regression when inline providers are removed from the distribution.\n58\t- The remote pgvector provider requires no OGX distribution code change; any gap found in the provider is documented and resolved within this epic (fix-and-retry).\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- REQ-1: default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual provisioning or configuration.\n63\t- REQ-2: playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store.\n64\t- REQ-4: default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n65\t- REQ-5: multi-tenant scoping per the selected model.\n66\t- REQ-6: lightweight resource footprint.\n67\t- REQ-10: portability toward the RHOAI 3.6 platform-provided shared PostgreSQL (operator pattern aligns with consuming a shared connection string).\n68\t\n69\t## Risks / Notes\n70\t\n71\t- Hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery timing; this branch exists only if that dependency lands in time for RHOAI 3.5.\n72\t- Epic size: ~1.5-2 sprints (qualitative — the strategy's effort arithmetic is unavailable); kept whole because provisioning and provider wiring for one approach form a single logical change over the same code paths. Re-split trigger: lifecycle-management work exceeds its design estimate by more than ~50%.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6e723cc7b26cd0d","agent_id":"aa8f64a754387b1a3","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"e7f40127-465a-45e1-a98e-0428e0def526","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:46:35.311Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-845f431deaf729c7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
