ayer slips → BFF-managed provisioning\n234\t  (BRANCH-B-E006, the preferred alternative per SE input); C — operator layer slips and\n235\t  BFF-managed is ruled out → customer-provided PostgreSQL (BRANCH-C-E006). Exactly one\n236\t  branch is implemented.\n237\t- **E003 (migration path) outcomes:** A — migration path affirmed → BRANCH-A-E007\n238\t  (implementation) plus BRANCH-A-E009 (user documentation); not affirmed → no epic\n239\t  (positioning guidance only, folded into the selected delivery branch's documentation\n240\t  scope).\n241\t- Branch epics are not standalone Jira issues; each branch's epics attach to the gating\n242\t  Investigation as a plan document. Branch epics are excluded from the main-plan\n243\t  critical path. `epic_count` counts all epics including branches (11); main-plan epics:\n244\t  5; main-plan critical path length: 2.\n245\t- Docs-authoring epics live inside their branches (BRANCH-C-E008 for the setup guide,\n246\t  BRANCH-A-E009 for the migration path); branch B's documentation needs are incidental\n247\t  touch-ups within its implementation epic. Per Rule 11 (docs-last), each docs epic is\n248\t  blocked by the main-plan Implementation epics and by the branch code epic whose\n249\t  delivered implementation it documents and is technically reviewed against.\n250\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f5e150208d747e","agent_id":"a5236c8cb9613bd11","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"2732d767-7d2f-4d20-89ac-123e2917c2c5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:53:27.903Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc5c74add5d16ec7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
