{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fb8ed57743ead92","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Go/no-go decision: RHOAI 3.5 default vector store provisioning approach'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Go/No-Go Decision: RHOAI 3.5 Default Vector Store Provisioning Approach\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves which provisioning approach ships the default PostgreSQL/pgvector vector store for the Gen AI Studio playground in RHOAI 3.5. Three bounded outcomes: (A) operator-based self-provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164); (B) gen-ai BFF-managed provisioning of the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance; or (C) requiring customers to bring their own PostgreSQL with manual OGXServer configuration. The outcome selects one of three conditional implementation branches and is recorded as the go/no-go gate the development team defines in sprint planning.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Confirm RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization, In Progress) delivery timing against the RHOAI 3.5 schedule — the hard dependency for operator-based self-provisioning, since the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry RHOAI-specific provisioning logic.\n34\t- Evaluate the two fallbacks if the operator layer is not ready in time: BFF-managed PostgreSQL provisioning (the preferred alternative) and customer-provided PostgreSQL with manual OGXServer CR configuration (aligned with the OGX 1.0 breaking-change posture).\n35\t- Define the go/no-go decision criteria and the sprint-planning checkpoint at which the gate is called.\n36\t- Produce a decision record: selected approach, rationale, risks, and portability implications toward the RHOAI 3.6 platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DSC.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A decision record exists naming the selected RHOAI 3.5 provisioning approach, with rationale grounded in the confirmed RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery status.\n41\t- The go/no-go gate criteria and checkpoint timing are documented and agreed in sprint planning.\n42\t- Each of the three possible outcomes has a defined conditional implementation branch (operator-based, BFF-managed, bring-your-own) so implementation can start immediately once the decision is made.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- REQ-9: go/no-go gate for the 3.5 approach defined as part of sprint planning (Staff Engineer Input).\n47\t- Enables REQ-1 (out-of-the-box default vector store) and REQ-8 (RHAISTRAT-7474 unblocked) by selecting the delivery approach.\n48\t\n49\t## Risks / Notes\n50\t\n51\t- Release-commitment risk: per the Staff Engineer Input, it will be challenging to commit this strategy to a specific release until RHAISTRAT-7164 is delivered; this decision epic exists precisely to manage that risk rather than let it silently block all work.\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f5e150208d747e","agent_id":"a5236c8cb9613bd11","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"ef56176d-69ee-4804-bbfc-3d2ed1173e2d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:53:32.307Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fb8ed57743ead92","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
