{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9820c7f183625659","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E004\n3\ttitle: Inline Milvus baseline and pgvector default vector store benchmark\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Inline Milvus Baseline and pgvector Default Vector Store Benchmark\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tCaptures the performance baseline of the current inline Milvus vector store provider and benchmarks the remote pgvector vector I/O provider against it on representative Gen AI Studio playground RAG workloads, verifying that pgvector is in the same order of magnitude. Also records PostgreSQL resource-sizing observations against the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource requests/limits starting point. This is Tier 1 risk-reduction work: it does not depend on the provisioning-approach decision, and the inline baseline must be captured while inline providers still exist in the OGX distribution image (they are removed by RHAISTRAT-7474).\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Capture the inline Milvus provider baseline on representative playground RAG workloads (typical usage involves small document sets).\n38\t- Benchmark the OGX remote pgvector vector I/O provider on the same workloads, backed by a standalone PostgreSQL/pgvector instance using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that already includes pgvector (no custom image build, no Konflux onboarding).\n39\t- Use flat scan (no index) for the default store — sufficient for development-experimentation usage; do not evaluate index-type selection or corpus-size ranges (resolved out of scope by Staff Engineer Input).\n40\t- Compare results: verify pgvector is in the same order of magnitude as the inline Milvus baseline; strict latency SLAs (p50/p95/p99 thresholds) are explicitly not required.\n41\t- Record resource-usage observations for PostgreSQL/pgvector sizing relative to the model-registry-operator's resource requests/limits reference.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- The benchmark report documents the inline Milvus baseline captured from the current inline provider while it is still available in the distribution image.\n46\t- The benchmark report documents pgvector measurements on identical workloads and states the same-order-of-magnitude comparison result.\n47\t- The benchmark report records resource-usage observations against the model-registry-operator PostgreSQL sizing reference.\n48\t- The benchmark harness (scripts, workload definitions, configuration) is retained and reproducible.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- REQ-6: default vector store lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments (sizing observations against the reference).\n53\t- Contributes to REQ-2: playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability (performance-parity evidence).\n54\t\n55\t## Risks / Notes\n56\t\n57\t- Cross-strategy timing risk: the inline Milvus baseline must be captured before RHAISTRAT-7474 removes inline providers from the OGX distribution image. If that removal lands first, reconstruct the baseline from a pinned pre-removal image.\n58\t- The sizing findings feed the provisioning implementations as an acceptance-criterion gate (resource requests/limits start from the model-registry-operator reference and are adjusted per these findings), not as a blocking dependency — the benchmark and the gated provisioning work run in parallel.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f5e150208d747e","agent_id":"a5236c8cb9613bd11","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"3caa7661-419a-441b-bc60-4d517ec40faa","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:53:36.021Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9820c7f183625659","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
