{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd69876e0613f02a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Operator-based self-provisioning of the default pgvector vector store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: 'If the RHOAI-controlled operator layer (RHAISTRAT-7164) does\n17\t    not land in time for RHOAI 3.5, provisioning moves to the BFF-managed or bring-your-own\n18\t    branch; the operator-based lifecycle design does not ship in 3.5 and may move\n19\t    to 3.6 aligned with the platform-provided shared database. The scoping-model investigation\n20\t    is a second true gate with rewrite semantics for this epic: if it lands on a different\n21\t    model, the provisioning topology (instance placement, isolation, lifecycle ownership)\n22\t    is rewritten to match.'\n23\tai_signals:\n24\t  change_specificity: 0\n25\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n26\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n27\t  existing_foundation: -1\n28\t  open_questions: -1\n29\t  external_dependency: -1\n30\t  human_process_gates: 0\n31\t  repo_access: 1\n32\t  architecture_claims: 1\n33\timplementation_type: null\n34\tinvestigation_signals: null\n35\tai_implementability: Medium\n36\tai_implementability_score: 1\n37\tjira_key: null\n38\t---\n39\t# Operator-Based Self-Provisioning of the Default pgvector Vector Store\n40\t\n41\t## Description\n42\t\n43\tDelivers the default vector store for the Gen AI Studio playground by extending the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer (delivered by the dashboard operator modularization, RHAISTRAT-7164) with PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management, following the model-registry-operator pattern: the operator provisions and manages a PostgreSQL instance — using the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that already includes pgvector (no custom image build, no Konflux onboarding) — and the gen-ai BFF configures playground OGXServer instances to use the remote pgvector vector I/O provider backed by it. This branch is selected when the go/no-go decision confirms the operator layer lands in time for RHOAI 3.5.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Operator-layer PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management (provisioning, connection-secret delivery, upgrades, cleanup) following the model-registry-operator pattern for auto-provisioned databases; the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry this RHOAI-specific logic.\n48\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that ships pgvector; resource requests/limits start from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing and are adjusted per the benchmark findings.\n49\t- Implement the scoping model selected by the scoping investigation (per-namespace isolation preferred).\n50\t- Gen-ai BFF wiring: playground OGXServer instances are configured with the remote pgvector vector I/O provider connected to the operator-provisioned database; OGX application storage remains on its existing SQLite default (vector storage and application storage are independent configurations — no consolidation, no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL application-storage migration).\n51\t- Reuse the existing OGX remote vector store implementation; no OGX distribution code change is expected, and provider behavior is validated as an acceptance criterion.\n52\t- Document the default store's positioning: development-experimentation grade, with production-scale vector workloads directed to an external vector database.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A PostgreSQL/pgvector instance is provisioned and managed by the operator, with credentials delivered via a secret; provisioning and cleanup happen without manual intervention.\n57\t- Playground OGXServer instances use the remote pgvector vector I/O provider backed by the provisioned database; OGX application storage remains SQLite.\n58\t- Resource requests/limits follow the model-registry-operator starting point, adjusted per the benchmark findings.\n59\t- Scoping follows the selected scoping model (per-namespace isolation unless the decision differs).\n60\t- Escape hatch / rollback path: the playground can be pointed at an externally provisioned vector database, so the default store is not a single point of regression when inline providers are removed from the distribution.\n61\t- The remote pgvector provider requires no OGX distribution code change; any gap found in the provider is documented and resolved within this epic (fix-and-retry).\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- REQ-1: default vector store available out-of-the-box without manual provisioning or configuration.\n66\t- REQ-2: playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store.\n67\t- REQ-4: default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n68\t- REQ-5: multi-tenant scoping per the selected model.\n69\t- REQ-6: lightweight resource footprint.\n70\t- REQ-10: portability toward the RHOAI 3.6 platform-provided shared PostgreSQL (operator pattern aligns with consuming a shared connection string).\n71\t\n72\t## Risks / Notes\n73\t\n74\t- Hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery timing; this branch exists only if that dependency lands in time for RHOAI 3.5.\n75\t- Epic size: ~1.5-2 sprints (qualitative — the strategy's effort arithmetic is unavailable); kept whole because provisioning and provider wiring for one approach form a single logical change over the same code paths. Re-split trigger: lifecycle-management work exceeds its design estimate by more than ~50%.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f5e150208d747e","agent_id":"a5236c8cb9613bd11","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"3bcd1031-2748-4852-a280-98d3bc51c0a2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:53:39.082Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd69876e0613f02a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
