{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83b873bdf5119808","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E006\n3\ttitle: Customer-provided PostgreSQL support for playground RAG\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: C\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: 'If the go/no-go decision selects a self-provisioning approach\n17\t    (operator-based or BFF-managed), this epic is not implemented; only the external-database\n18\t    escape-hatch support may be retained as part of the selected branch. The scoping-model\n19\t    investigation is a second true gate with rewrite semantics for this epic: if it\n20\t    lands on a different model, the provisioning topology (instance placement, isolation,\n21\t    lifecycle ownership) is rewritten to match.'\n22\tai_signals:\n23\t  change_specificity: 1\n24\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n25\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n26\t  existing_foundation: 1\n27\t  open_questions: -1\n28\t  external_dependency: 1\n29\t  human_process_gates: 0\n30\t  repo_access: 1\n31\t  architecture_claims: 1\n32\timplementation_type: null\n33\tinvestigation_signals: null\n34\tai_implementability: High\n35\tai_implementability_score: 5\n36\tjira_key: null\n37\t---\n38\t# Customer-Provided PostgreSQL Support for Playground RAG\n39\t\n40\t## Description\n41\t\n42\tDegraded fallback for RHOAI 3.5, selected only if the go/no-go decision rules out both self-provisioning approaches: require customers to bring their own PostgreSQL for RAG capabilities in the playground. Users manually configure the OGXServer CR spec with their PostgreSQL connection details — aligning with the breaking changes introduced in OGX 1.0 — while the playground continues to abstract OGX from users where possible. This branch deliberately does not preserve the out-of-the-box experience; that degradation is accepted explicitly by the go/no-go decision.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Support user-supplied PostgreSQL connection details (explicit connection string secret) on playground OGXServer instances, with the remote pgvector vector I/O provider configured against the user's database.\n47\t- Surface actionable validation and errors in the playground when connection details are missing or invalid (playground RAG requires a vector store once inline providers are removed from the distribution).\n48\t- User documentation for the setup is authored as separate docs-authoring work within this branch and technically reviewed against this implementation; only incidental doc touch-ups land here.\n49\t- Document positioning guidance: the default-store capability is development-experimentation grade, and guidance for choosing a production-grade vector database.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A user-configured PostgreSQL connection (supplied via secret) is honored by the playground's OGXServer instance, and playground RAG workflows function against it.\n54\t- Missing or invalid connection configuration produces actionable feedback in the playground.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- REQ-2: playground RAG workflows function (with the user-provided vector store).\n59\t- REQ-4: the vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n60\t- Partial REQ-1/REQ-7 coverage only, by design: this branch accepts manual setup as the documented 3.5 fallback per the Staff Engineer Input; the out-of-the-box experience is restored by the platform-provided shared database direction in RHOAI 3.6.\n61\t\n62\t## Risks / Notes\n63\t\n64\t- This branch exists only if the go/no-go decision selects the bring-your-own fallback; it is the last-resort outcome, not the preferred one.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f5e150208d747e","agent_id":"a5236c8cb9613bd11","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"fb75e874-2e7b-4382-81cf-bb19f512f462","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:53:40.415Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-83b873bdf5119808","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
