ase, or data export), at the functional level the decision specifies.\n44\t- Align with the commonly-used vector DB providers supported by the OGX vector I/O provider surface (pgvector, Milvus, Qdrant backends).\n45\t- User documentation for the migration path is authored as separate docs-authoring work within this branch and technically reviewed against this implementation; only incidental doc touch-ups land here.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- The affirmed migration form works end to end for a representative playground document set.\n50\t- The migration is exercised against an instance delivered by the selected provisioning approach — the default store shipped under the outcome of the go/no-go decision (this coupling to the selected delivery is an acceptance gate on this epic, alongside its dependency on the go/no-go decision).\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- REQ-11: migration path from the default vector store to a production-grade vector database.\n55\t\n56\t## Risks / Notes\n57\t\n58\t- Scope is conditional on the migration-path decision; the decision record is the authoritative specification of the migration form.\n59\t- Coupled to the go/no-go provisioning-approach decision: if the bring-your-own outcome is selected, no default store ships and there is nothing to migrate from — neither this implementation nor its documentation exists in that outcome.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f5e150208d747e","agent_id":"a5236c8cb9613bd11","session_id":"172d32aa-435a-4a07-8b59-185510da7cc9","uuid":"91f3a94d-4df3-48e9-a6b1-81fef3693e37","timestamp":"2026-10-26T22:53:42.776Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3a60ad65bd50629","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
